# Example 39: 3D LBM biofilm - D3Q19 microfluidic channel
# (Design 6 Level 2 3D, doc/18-programmable-cell-population-simulation.md §13)
# A colony of cells grows inside a 3D pressure-driven channel.  Every
# tick the D3Q19 lattice-Boltzmann solver recomputes the 3D flow around
# the cells (no-slip obstacles); the refreshed FlowField3D drives 3D
# cell drift (lattice sites move along the axial current) and, when a
# #media block is present, 3D substrate advection.  `#sim lbm_3d=true`
# is the 3D counterpart of `#sim lbm=true` (D2Q9) and requires
# grid_depth > 1.

#promoter name=p_housekeeping strength=-0.4

#gene name=pilT promoter=p_housekeeping
ATG GCT GGT GCT TAA
#end

#config backend=population
#config population_size=27 grid_width=16 grid_height=16 grid_depth=8
#sim lbm_3d=true relaxation_omega=1.2 lbm_substeps=3
#config signaling=true signal_diffusion=0.3 signal_threshold=20.0
#config seed=0
#config ticks=10
#config output=alive_count,diversity_index,avg_energy
